test.yaml:7:14: "npm install" resolves the dependencies again and may update the package-lock.json instead of failing when it is out of date. use `npm ci` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:7:14: "npm install" runs the lifecycle scripts (preinstall, install, postinstall) of every dependency, and a compromised release uses them to run code on the runner. pass `--ignore-scripts` or set `ignore-scripts=true` in .npmrc, and run what a package needs with `npm rebuild` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:7:14: "npm install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. pass `--min-release-age=7` or set `min-release-age=7` in .npmrc (npm 11.10 and later) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:8:14: "npm i" resolves the dependencies again and may update the package-lock.json instead of failing when it is out of date. use `npm ci` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:8:14: "npm i" runs the lifecycle scripts (preinstall, install, postinstall) of every dependency, and a compromised release uses them to run code on the runner. pass `--ignore-scripts` or set `ignore-scripts=true` in .npmrc, and run what a package needs with `npm rebuild` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:8:14: "npm i" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. pass `--min-release-age=7` or set `min-release-age=7` in .npmrc (npm 11.10 and later) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:9:14: "yarn" does not require the yarn.lock to be up to date in Yarn 1, and relies on the CI detection of Yarn 2+. pass `--immutable` (`--frozen-lockfile` for Yarn 1) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:9:14: "yarn" runs the lifecycle scripts (preinstall, install, postinstall) of every dependency, and a compromised release uses them to run code on the runner. pass `--ignore-scripts` (`--mode=skip-build` in Yarn 2+) or set `enableScripts: false` in .yarnrc.yml [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:9:14: "yarn" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. set `npmMinimalAgeGate` in .yarnrc.yml (Yarn 4.10 and later, Yarn 1 has no such setting) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:10:14: "yarn install" does not require the yarn.lock to be up to date in Yarn 1, and relies on the CI detection of Yarn 2+. pass `--immutable` (`--frozen-lockfile` for Yarn 1) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:10:14: "yarn install" runs the lifecycle scripts (preinstall, install, postinstall) of every dependency, and a compromised release uses them to run code on the runner. pass `--ignore-scripts` (`--mode=skip-build` in Yarn 2+) or set `enableScripts: false` in .yarnrc.yml [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:10:14: "yarn install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. set `npmMinimalAgeGate` in .yarnrc.yml (Yarn 4.10 and later, Yarn 1 has no such setting) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:11:14: "bun install" may update bun.lock instead of failing when it is out of date. use `bun ci` or pass `--frozen-lockfile` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:11:14: "bun install" runs the lifecycle scripts of the packages on the default trusted list of bun, and a compromised release of one of them uses them to run code on the runner. pass `--ignore-scripts`, or list the packages that need them in "trustedDependencies" of package.json (a list replaces the default one) [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:11:14: "bun install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. set `minimumReleaseAge` (in seconds, bun 1.3 and later) under `[install]` in bunfig.toml [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:12:14: "pnpm install" is told not to freeze the lock file, so it may update pnpm-lock.yaml instead of failing when it is out of date. pass --frozen-lockfile [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:12:14: "pnpm install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. set `minimumReleaseAge` (in minutes, pnpm 10.16 and later) in pnpm-workspace.yaml [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:13:14: "pnpm install" is told not to freeze the lock file, so it may update pnpm-lock.yaml instead of failing when it is out of date. pass --frozen-lockfile [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:14:14: "pip install -r requirements.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:14:14: "pip install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. pass `--uploaded-prior-to` (pip 26.0 and later; a date, or a duration such as `P7D`), or install with uv and `--exclude-newer` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:15:14: "pip3 install -r requirements/dev.txt -r requirements/test.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:15:14: "pip3 install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. pass `--uploaded-prior-to` (pip 26.0 and later; a date, or a duration such as `P7D`), or install with uv and `--exclude-newer` [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:16:14: "uv pip install -r requirements.txt" installs a requirements file without hashes or constraints, so the transitive dependencies are resolved anew on every run. use a lock file with hashes (`pip-compile --generate-hashes`) and pass --require-hashes, or pin them with -c [unlocked-install]
test.yaml:16:14: "uv pip install" takes the newest release of every dependency, however new, so a compromised release reaches the workflow before it is found and pulled. pass `--exclude-newer` with a duration (`--exclude-newer "7 days"`) or a date, or set `exclude-newer` in uv.toml [unlocked-install]
